{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WafjjDG9WoHeZmma8KV61E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd082-stat\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/stat: Display File Status\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD stat that differs from GNU stat in default output format, format\n6\t  string syntax, and flag names. GNU stat supports printf-style format strings for\n7\t  customizable output. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n8\t  (gstat, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n9\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Display file status information (size, permissions, timestamps, inode, etc.).\n13\t  - G2: Support printf-style format strings for custom output via --format (-c).\n14\t  - G3: Support filesystem status mode via --file-system (-f).\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gstat via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Default file status\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must display file status for each named file argument using the default multi-line format matching GNU stat output (File, Size, Blocks, IO Block, file type, Device, Inode, Links, Access mode, Uid, Gid, Access time, Modify time, Change time, Birth time).\n23\t\n24\t  R2:\n25\t    title: File listing options\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R2.1:\n28\t          text: Must process multiple file arguments in order, printing status for each.\n29\t      - R2.2:\n30\t          text: \"-L or --dereference must follow symlinks and report the target file's status instead of the link itself.\"\n31\t      - R2.3:\n32\t          text: Must exit 1 when any named file does not exist or cannot be accessed, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n33\t\n34\t  R3:\n35\t    title: Format strings\n36\t    items:\n37\t      - R3.1:\n38\t          text: \"-c FORMAT or --format=FORMAT must use FORMAT as a printf-style format string. Must support directives: %a (access rights octal), %A (access rights human), %b (blocks allocated), %B (block size), %d (device number decimal), %D (device number hex), %f (raw mode hex), %F (file type), %g (group ID), %G (group name), %h (hard links), %i (inode), %m (mount point), %n (file name), %N (quoted file name with symlink target), %o (optimal I/O size), %s (total size bytes), %t (major device type hex), %T (minor device type hex), %u (user ID), %U (user name), %w (birth time human), %W (birth time epoch), %x (access time human), %X (access time epoch), %y (modify time human), %Y (modify time epoch), %z (change time human), %Z (change time epoch).\"\n39\t\n40\t  R4:\n41\t    title: Printf and terse output\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R4.1:\n44\t          text: \"--printf=FORMAT must work like --format but interpret backslash escapes (\\\\n, \\\\t, etc.) and not append a trailing newline.\"\n45\t      - R4.2:\n46\t          text: \"-t or --terse must produce terse output (single line of space-separated fields) matching GNU stat --terse format.\"\n47\t\n48\t  R5:\n49\t    title: Filesystem status\n50\t    items:\n51\t      - R5.1:\n52\t          text: \"-f or --file-system must display filesystem status instead of file status. Output includes filesystem type, block size, total/free/available blocks and inodes.\"\n53\t\n54\t  R6:\n55\t    title: Filesystem format directives\n56\t    items:\n57\t      - R6.1:\n58\t          text: \"Format directives in --file-system mode differ from file mode: %a (free blocks available to non-root), %b (total blocks), %c (total inodes), %d (free inodes), %f (free blocks), %i (filesystem ID hex), %l (max filename length), %n (file name), %s (block size optimal), %S (fundamental block size), %t (filesystem type hex), %T (filesystem type name).\"\n59\t\n60\t  R7:\n61\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n62\t    items:\n63\t      - R7.1:\n64\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n65\t      - R7.2:\n66\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or an invalid format directive is used.\n67\t      - R7.3:\n68\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n69\t\n70\tnon_goals:\n71\t  - cmd/stat does not implement SELinux context display (--context).\n72\t\n73\tacceptance_criteria:\n74\t  - id: AC1\n75\t    criterion: \"stat on a regular file produces multi-line status output matching gstat.\"\n76\t    traces:\n77\t      - R1.1\n78\t      - R2.1\n79\t      - R2.3\n80\t  - id: AC2\n81\t    criterion: \"stat -c '%s %n' file produces size and name, matching gstat -c '%s %n'.\"\n82\t    traces:\n83\t      - R3.1\n84\t  - id: AC3\n85\t    criterion: \"stat -f / produces filesystem status matching gstat -f /.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R5.1\n88\t      - R6.1\n89\t  - id: AC4\n90\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gstat passes for all required test cases.\"\n91\t    traces:\n92\t      - R1.1\n93\t      - R3.1\n94\t      - R5.1\n95\t  - id: AC5\n96\t    criterion: \"cmd/stat compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n97\t    traces:\n98\t      - R1.1\n99\t      - R2.1\n100\t      - R2.2\n101\t      - R2.3\n102\t      - R3.1\n103\t      - R4.1\n104\t      - R4.2\n105\t      - R5.1\n106\t      - R6.1\n107\t      - R7.1\n108\t      - R7.2\n109\t      - R7.3\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f82c57d2-d156-47af-9634-ce60dffa6178","uuid":"e5372464-ba2c-4009-8d31-8a6c960b0ced","timestamp":"2026-05-23T15:20:13.196Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5534/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd082-stat.yaml","content":"id: srd082-stat\ntitle: \"cmd/stat: Display File Status\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD stat that differs from GNU stat in default output format, format\n  string syntax, and flag names. GNU stat supports printf-style format strings for\n  customizable output. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n  (gstat, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Display file status information (size, permissions, timestamps, inode, etc.).\n  - G2: Support printf-style format strings for custom output via --format (-c).\n  - G3: Support filesystem status mode via --file-system (-f).\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gstat via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default file status\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must display file status for each named file argument using the default multi-line format matching GNU stat output (File, Size, Blocks, IO Block, file type, Device, Inode, Links, Access mode, Uid, Gid, Access time, Modify time, Change time, Birth time).\n\n  R2:\n    title: File listing options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must process multiple file arguments in order, printing status for each.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-L or --dereference must follow symlinks and report the target file's status instead of the link itself.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any named file does not exist or cannot be accessed, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Format strings\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-c FORMAT or --format=FORMAT must use FORMAT as a printf-style format string. Must support directives: %a (access rights octal), %A (access rights human), %b (blocks allocated), %B (block size), %d (device number decimal), %D (device number hex), %f (raw mode hex), %F (file type), %g (group ID), %G (group name), %h (hard links), %i (inode), %m (mount point), %n (file name), %N (quoted file name with symlink target), %o (optimal I/O size), %s (total size bytes), %t (major device type hex), %T (minor device type hex), %u (user ID), %U (user name), %w (birth time human), %W (birth time epoch), %x (access time human), %X (access time epoch), %y (modify time human), %Y (modify time epoch), %z (change time human), %Z (change time epoch).\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Printf and terse output\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"--printf=FORMAT must work like --format but interpret backslash escapes (\\\\n, \\\\t, etc.) and not append a trailing newline.\"\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"-t or --terse must produce terse output (single line of space-separated fields) matching GNU stat --terse format.\"\n\n  R5:\n    title: Filesystem status\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: \"-f or --file-system must display filesystem status instead of file status. Output includes filesystem type, block size, total/free/available blocks and inodes.\"\n\n  R6:\n    title: Filesystem format directives\n    items:\n      - R6.1:\n          text: \"Format directives in --file-system mode differ from file mode: %a (free blocks available to non-root), %b (total blocks), %c (total inodes), %d (free inodes), %f (free blocks), %i (filesystem ID hex), %l (max filename length), %n (file name), %s (block size optimal), %S (fundamental block size), %t (filesystem type hex), %T (filesystem type name).\"\n\n  R7:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R7.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R7.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or an invalid format directive is used.\n      - R7.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/stat does not implement SELinux context display (--context).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"stat on a regular file produces multi-line status output matching gstat.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"stat -c '%s %n' file produces size and name, matching gstat -c '%s %n'.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"stat -f / produces filesystem status matching gstat -f /.\"\n    traces:\n      - R5.1\n      - R6.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gstat passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R3.1\n      - R5.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/stat compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R5.1\n      - R6.1\n      - R7.1\n      - R7.2\n      - R7.3\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1,"totalLines":110}}}
